        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "05bb8e11-7342-522b-88bd-dcdcf1ff612c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Andrey Zvyagintsev, Marvin Heemeyer, Naboth\n- Works: Leviathan (2014 film)\n- Places: United States, Russia, Granby, Colorado\n- Concepts: Naboth's Vineyard\n- Events: Granby bulldozer rampage\n\nFacts:\n- On June 4, 2004, Marvin Heemeyer, an automobile muffler repair shop owner, drove an armored bulldozer through Granby, Colorado, damaging 13 buildings and causing about $7 million in damage.\n- According to Andrey Zvyagintsev, the story of Marvin Heemeyer in the United States inspired Leviathan (2014 film), and Zvyagintsev adapted that inspiration into a Russian setting.\n- Critics compared Leviathan (2014 film) to the biblical story of Naboth's Vineyard, in which a king seeks a subject's land and is urged by his queen to obtain it slyly.",
